-- ============================================================================
-- PD2 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Gas Lift Design, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE VALVES. Where they go, what they are set to, and
-- what a setting asserts.
--
-- SPACING IS A RECURSION, NOT A FORMULA. Valve 1 sits where the injection line
-- first overcomes a full column of kill fluid. Every valve after it sits where
-- the injection line, decremented by the surface drop per valve, still beats
-- the transfer pressure at the valve above by the transfer differential, with
-- kill fluid in between. Change the decrement and every depth BELOW the change
-- moves while every depth above it stays put. That is why a design is a string
-- and not a list of valves, and it is why the two spacing conventions are one
-- recursion with a different decrement rather than two methods.
--
-- A FAILS-OPEN, AND IT IS WORSE THAN "EXEMPT". In `spaceValves` the
-- target-depth branch breaks BEFORE the minimum spacing check. On the
-- published westTexasOil case the valve 8 recursion had ALREADY converged to a
-- 206.016771390 ft increment against a stated 250 ft minimum before the
-- mandrel was pulled to its floor, so the design had reached the condition
-- that says STOP and a mandrel was seated anyway, 131.375432376 ft from its
-- neighbour, with no warning. constantPressurePPO does the same at
-- 152.956208919 ft against 200 ft. Two of the four published cases exercise
-- it, and THE ORACLE ORDERS THE SAME TWO BRANCHES THE SAME WAY, so the golden
-- records agreement where neither side ever reached the test.
--
-- ONE ROOT CAUSE WITH TWO SYMPTOMS, PINNED AND NOT FIXED. `valveSpread` is
-- handed `pOpen = pProd` and `pOtherSide = pInj` for a production operated
-- valve, which is the two sides swapped. That single line produces a NEGATIVE
-- spread on every valve of the published PPO case, between -52.249540846 and
-- -31.296561503 psi, and it is the same line that makes
-- `closingSurfacePressurePsia` judge a production operated string against the
-- CASING: the engine clears the casing side threshold by 379.101060 to
-- 724.986977 psi while the tubing side rule it should be judged by misses by
-- 31.822047 to 52.249541 psi on every valve. Not fixed, because the engine is
-- consumed by a live Suite app.
--
-- Worth teaching for its own sake: the LOUD symptom went unremarked. A spread
-- is a pressure fall, so a negative one is not a valve property and cannot be
-- anything but an argument order, and it is the subtler closing verdict that
-- somebody actually reported.
--
-- AND A MECHANISM THAT IS NOT A SLOPE. The multipointing verdict reaches the
-- design gas rate ONLY through `selectPort`, so it moves in catalogue STEPS:
-- frozen at 0.124769727 psi of stage 5 margin from 400 through 1400 Mscf/d,
-- then jumping to 15.249903355 psi at 1600 with an extra multipointing stage.
-- A coarse sweep steps over the flip and a fine one finds nothing between the
-- steps and feels like evidence. A sweep's resolution has to match the
-- MECHANISM and not the axis.
-- ============================================================================

